This roadmap is better aligned with a classified and peer-to-peer marketplace where users sell both new and pre-owned items, while still leaving room to support professional stores and businesses alongside individual sellers.
At the start of every new phase, use a prompt like this:

"Implement Phase X completely. Analyze the existing project first. Preserve the current customer-facing UI exactly as it is unless a new feature requires a minimal addition. You may redesign the admin and seller portals for better usability and scalability. Generate production-ready code only—no placeholders, no TODOs, no pseudocode. Fully implement frontend, backend, database migrations, APIs, validation, authentication, authorization, tests, documentation, and responsive UI. If the response reaches the output limit, continue automatically from the exact point where it stopped until the phase is fully complete."
